<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ōrākau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/invasion-of-the-waikato">Invasion of the Waikato</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ōrākau was fought from 31 March to 2 April 1864 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikato">Waikato</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, the last major battle of the British invasion of the Waikato. About 300 Māori under Rewi Maniapoto, including women, defended a hastily built pā against a much larger British force. Refusing to surrender, they broke out and many were killed. The battle ended organised resistance in the Waikato.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-orakau.jpg" alt="Battle of Ōrākau" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Cowan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ngati_maniapoto_survivors_of_the_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
